   "daf": "99b",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "וְאֵינוֹ חוֹלֵק לֶאֱכוֹל כּוּ׳. מִיפְלָג הוּא דְּלָא פְּלִיג, וְכִי מְזַמְּנִי לֵיהּ – אָכֵיל;",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches with regard to an acute mourner: «And he does not receive a share» of sacrificial meat in order «to partake» of it in the evening. The Gemara comments: The mishna indicates only that «he may not receive a share» of the meat, «but when» other priests «invite him» to join in their portions, «he may partake» of them in the evening."
  }
